hese-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:18:34-07:00","id":886328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=885915#post885915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually back in First and second edition that's exactly what happened.<br /> <br /> That said, they'll have some sort of &quot;Curse&quot; or &quot;Problem&quot; mechanic, just like other Exalted who don't suffer from the Great Curse (Alchemical and Infernals). I'm sure each Exigent will probably have some sort of unique trigger and and such that reflects her own power and system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that they suffer from some sort of Resonance effect that aligns them with their patron(s). A god of a city would probably not want their Exigent wandering off and would want a way to encourage them to not go off adventuring without permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:23:45-07:00","id":886332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886328#post886328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine that they suffer from some sort of Resonance effect that aligns them with their patron(s). A god of a city would probably not want their Exigent wandering off and would want a way to encourage them to not go off adventuring without permission.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a god that survived the creation of its Exigent, maybe....but how about the ones that were created at the expense of the gods existence like the one with the scythe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:27:41-07:00","id":886337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886332#post886332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a god that survived the creation of its Exigent, maybe....but how about the ones that were created at the expense of the gods existence like the one with the scythe?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would probably be weaker than Celestial Exalted and would be the equivalent of Terrestrial Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:32:26-07:00","id":886342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886328#post886328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that they suffer from some sort of Resonance effect that aligns them with their patron(s). A god of a city would probably not want their Exigent wandering off and would want a way to encourage them to not go off adventuring without permission.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception of Abyssals (and even they're looking likely to get changed), the gods generally don't control the actions of their Chosen so directly. Or really at all for the most part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886337#post886337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would probably be weaker than Celestial Exalted and would be the equivalent of Terrestrial Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That directly contradicts Vance's earlier statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-09-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:38:10-07:00","id":886415,"title":"","content":"Well, until we get something in print, everything is subject to change. I imagine, however, that a god that was too weak to survive the creation an Exigent would produce an Exigent that was less powerful than a god that was strong enough to survive the creation of an Exigent (if nothing else, the Exigent of a dead god would lack any support structure). Of course, it would help out if the rules made each Exigent equally capable to other Exigents, but I really doubt that they will be as powerful as the Celestial Exalted. A question though, could a Lesser Elemental Dragon create an Exigent, even though they are not technically a god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:41:29-07:00","id":886421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine, however, that a god that was too weak to survive the creation an Exigent would produce an Exigent that was less powerful than a god that was strong enough to survive the creation of an Exigent</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be that the power of an Exigent comes from need and worth and the good will of the Unconquered Sun. That for a lowly field god to scrape and beg and sacrifice an immortal existence for the sake of a beloved land and valued people is something reflected in a warrior of particularly fearsome might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Exigent of a dead god would lack any support structure</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless that god leaves behind an order of loyal and highly trained warrior-priestesses who think that the one he gave himself up to empower is worthy of a transfer of their devotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886415#post886415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, it would help out if the rules made each Exigent equally capable to other Exigents, but I really doubt that they will be as powerful as the Celestial Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The developer of the game has said that it is possible for there to be Exigents to be around the same power as the Solar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-09-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:51:23-07:00","id":886436,"title":"","content":"I guess that would be what happens when a moderately powerful god goes all-in and sacrifices themselves or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:10:15-07:00","id":886462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886421#post886421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The developer of the game has said that it is possible for there to be Exigents to be around the same power as the Solar Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, but everything is subject to change until it is printed. We will likely not see an Exigent book until 2019, so they may decide to change their mind. Even if Exigents the equivalent of the Solar Exalted could be created, how would that effect the game world if there could potentially be hundreds (or thousands) of Exigents with the power of Celestial Exalted running around?<br /> <br /> One reason why I am nervous about the Exigents is that I see no logical reason why the Yozis could not reverse engineer the process of creating new Exalted if the Exigence exists, since the Exigence seems to create new Exalted essences. If the Exigence is capable of creating new Exalted Essences, why could the Yozis not use a similar method to allow their subsidiary souls to create their own Demonic Exigents? While they would still want Solar Exalted essences to deprive TUS of Solar Exalted, I would imagine that they would want a Demonic Exigence to allow their subsidiary souls to create a hundred Demonic Exigents for every Infernal Exalted that they possess.<br /> <br /> Of course, that could be an interesting story idea. There are a minimum of eighteen Yozis who are not part of the Reclamation of Creation but, with the introduction of the Infernal Exalted in Malfeas, they would want to improve their positions in Creation. I imagine that Cytherea, an entity so feared by the First Age Solar Exalted that they remove her name from practically every occult record, could reverse engineer the Exigence since she helped make Creation and, by extension, the Incarna that created the Exigence. She could then offer access to the Demonic Exigence to any of her siblings' subsidiary souls that are will to pay the price.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, the average Yozi possesses a couple dozen Third Circle Demons as its subsidiary souls and each Third Circle Demon possesses seven Second Circle Demons as their subsidiary souls. Each Fetich is equal in power to an Incarna, so I would think that they could produce around twenty Demonic Exigents without difficulty, while the remaining Third Circle Demons are equal in power to the greatest of gods, so I would think that they could produce around five Demonic Exigents without difficulty. The Second Circle Demons are the equivalent of major gods, so they could probably create a single Demonic Exigent without difficulty. That would mean that there could be potentially fifty-five hundred or so Demonic Exigents that could be active in Creation after the reserve engineering of the Exigence by Cytherea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:11:45-07:00","id":886464,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that all the new guys just won't get the Great Curse, and the developers will just sort of avoid making them anything like the Exalted-you-would-really-want-in-charge-because-they're-not-cursed in other ways than by having them *also* be cursed.<br /> <br /> The Doylist explanation for why the Solars get the Great Curse is to make them the excellent and flawed heroes of tragic epic, or if not that, heroic melodrama. Then the other traditional Exalted do too, to an extent, to partake in the same genre, in distinct ways that are marked by their originating power. The Alchemicals, on the other hand, don't, because they aren't - they just aren't the cyborg guys who get overwhelmed by eruptions of passionate human virtue (not that this wouldn't be a cool thing, Alchemicals aren't really it, unless that's what you decide about *your* Alchemical's personality).<br /> <br /> Now, if the Exigents are, as a general group, playing with the same theme as the Solars (and Dragonblooded and Lunars and Sidereals), and at being the same kind of heroes, ones who risk being undone by their own tempers, appetites, principles, strengths, emotions, then they might at least generally get the same cursed nature. It not, not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:14:05-07:00","id":886471,"title":"","content":"Word of &quot;God&quot; is that &quot;There has never been more than 300 Exigents at once, and the actual number is probably far, far fewer than that.&quot; (<a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:17:43-07:00","id":886476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886462#post886462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason why I am nervous about the Exigents is that I see no logical reason why the Yozis could not reverse engineer the process of creating new Exalted if the Exigence exists, since the Exigence seems to create new Exalted essences. If the Exigence is capable of creating new Exalted Essences, why could the Yozis not use a similar method to allow their subsidiary souls to create their own Demonic Exigents? While they would still want Solar Exalted essences to deprive TUS of Solar Exalted, I would imagine that they would want a Demonic Exigence to allow their subsidiary souls to create a hundred Demonic Exigents for every Infernal Exalted that they possess.</div> </div> </div> </div>They tried that. Due to the Law of Diminishment, it uh... it didn't go well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Infernals Preview from like, forever ago</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But after the Yozis were imprisoned, some began to disbelieve Autochthon\u2019s gambit, even as they realized that the Exalted were their only hope of escape. Oramus, the Dragon Beyond the World, and Isidoros, the Black Boar That Twists the Sky both tried to make their own Exalted, and the Yozis were disquieted by the results.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:19:54-07:00","id":886479,"title":"","content":"I thought that the theme of an Exigent came from their patron, but the power of their exaltation came from Sol?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Gods, why when I open a thread, does only half of the thread appear until after I have replied to it? I cannot believe that in the time it took to type 1 sentence, 12 people posted an entire page of multi-paragraph replies. D: Makes me look like an idiot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:16:57-07:00","id":886631,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Exigence is a force of divine fire and creative inspiration established by the Unconquered Sun<br /> so that lesser gods might have their own Exalted champions. Gods who tap the Exigence do not learn the secret of<br /> making Exalted, but through interaction with the Sun\u2019s medium, they are able to exude new kinds of Chosen from<br /> their own unique Essence. Some gods who petition to create an Exigent are destroyed by the process; they are simply<br /> too weak to produce a Chosen without spending their own lives. Others are powerful enough to make a single champion,<br /> though this effort leaves them drained and vastly reduced for a time. Still others may produce<br /> a single Exigent without wavering, while a truly mighty god might bring forth multiple heroes from his own Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is a mixture of the power of their patron and the Exigence of the Unconquered Sun. I think that the Exigence is a portion of the Wyld transformed by the power of the Unconquered Sun, though I may be incorrect. I do not think that the Exaltation comes from the Unconquered Sun, just that the Unconquered Sun provides the medium for the Exigence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:33:59-07:00","id":886736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886415#post886415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, until we get something in print, everything is subject to change. I imagine, however, that a god that was too weak to survive the creation an Exigent would produce an Exigent that was less powerful than a god that was strong enough to survive the creation of an Exigent (if nothing else, the Exigent of a dead god would lack any support structure). Of course, it would help out if the rules made each Exigent equally capable to other Exigents, but I really doubt that they will be as powerful as the Celestial Exalted. A question though, could a Lesser Elemental Dragon create an Exigent, even though they are not technically a god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think you are forgetting the possibility of a weaker god who gives their all to create as strong an Exigent as they can vs. the more powerful god who fears becoming nothing and holds back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:37:12-07:00","id":886740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886631#post886631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Exigence is a force of divine fire and creative inspiration established by the Unconquered Sun<br /> so that lesser gods might have their own Exalted champions. Gods who tap the Exigence do not learn the secret of<br /> making Exalted, but through interaction with the Sun\u2019s medium, they are able to exude new kinds of Chosen from<br /> their own unique Essence. Some gods who petition to create an Exigent are destroyed by the process; they are simply<br /> too weak to produce a Chosen without spending their own lives. Others are powerful enough to make a single champion,<br /> though this effort leaves them drained and vastly reduced for a time. Still others may produce<br /> a single Exigent without wavering, while a truly mighty god might bring forth multiple heroes from his own Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is a mixture of the power of their patron and the Exigence of the Unconquered Sun. I think that the Exigence is a portion of the Wyld transformed by the power of the Unconquered Sun, though I may be incorrect. I do not think that the Exaltation comes from the Unconquered Sun, just that the Unconquered Sun provides the medium for the Exigence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flat what. Why would the Wyld have anything to do with this process?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:56:18-07:00","id":886752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886462#post886462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One reason why I am nervous about the Exigents is that I see no logical reason why the Yozis could not reverse engineer the process of creating new Exalted if the Exigence exists, since the Exigence seems to create new Exalted essences.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bEven assuming that could be a thing, the Yozis have probably lacked access.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:12:15-07:00","id":886767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886740#post886740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Flat what. Why would the Wyld have anything to do with this process?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least in 2e, the energy of the Unconquered Sun was created by converting the essence of the Wyld into the essence of Creation, so I would think that the energy for the Exigence would have to come from the Wyld. The Wyld is the source of everything in Creation, it is the beginning and the end. That is one of the possible reasons why the Malfeans wanted Creation to be consumed by the Wyld, as it would have resurrected them and allowed them to transform their kin trapped in Malfeas back into Primordials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:20:32-07:00","id":886773,"title":"","content":"I assume that, as the Exaltation is a miracle, the outcome of a god creating an Exigent is impossible to fully predict. There may have been occasions where weak gods made multiple Exigents with nary an ill effect and other times where extremely powerful gods completely burned themselves out just making one.<br /> <br /> While there are probably general guidelines about the process of Exalting an Exigent, I hope we never get black and white, concrete absolutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:34:13-07:00","id":886787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886767#post886767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, at least in 2e, the energy of the Unconquered Sun was created by converting the essence of the Wyld into the essence of Creation, so I would think that the energy for the Exigence would have to come from the Wyld. The Wyld is the source of everything in Creation, it is the beginning and the end. That is one of the possible reasons why the Malfeans wanted Creation to be consumed by the Wyld, as it would have resurrected them and allowed them to transform their kin trapped in Malfeas back into Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neverborn resurrection was sketchy and highly optional even in second edition. Drawing energy off the Wyld the way Glories had it runs into the problem of a lot of Glories by necessity having to be moved out of the field of view at minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:49:04-07:00","id":886801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886767#post886767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, at least in 2e, the energy of the Unconquered Sun was created by converting the essence of the Wyld into the essence of Creation, so I would think that the energy for the Exigence would have to come from the Wyld. The Wyld is the source of everything in Creation, it is the beginning and the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like saying that sorcerers need food to live, so all spells must have some kind of core of food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:49:21-07:00","id":886840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886801#post886801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is like saying that sorcerers need food to live, so all spells must have some kind of core of food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are made out of meat... usually. (^VVVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:14:09-07:00","id":886860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/885839-are-exigents-affected-by-the-great-curse?p=886057#post886057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ex3 is kind of inconsistent on this point, actually.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer to believe that it was against both gods and Chosen. And that the gods probably didn't thwart it, even if they think they did. I mean, look at how the Incarnae behave these days...</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively: &quot;May you know the betrayal we have known&quot;<br /> <br /> It didn't miss. Rooting in the heart of the Chosen is exactly how it will eventually destroy the Incarnae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T20:54:21-07:00","id":888814,"title":"","content":"My take on it would be that if there were any Exigents in Primordial War, they got cursed, but not any Exigents made afterwords, because Exigents are individuals, not the great collectives of the celestial exalts, not the terrestrial bloodlines, but unique individuals, who have never appeared before, and never will again.<br /> <br /> They probably have some equivalent mechanically, the way that Abyssals and Infernals had their own, but they they don't have the big 'C' Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:56:44-07:00","id":889209,"title":"","content":"I would guess that Exigents will have features more similar to Fetters than Limit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"